  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Every member has access to one modest storage allowance, and all project containers must identify their owner and next review date.\", \"decision\": \"How should unfinished projects be stored between sessions?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward assigns an available shelf position when members present packed unfinished projects with review dates. A central placement record makes projects easy to locate without changing each member’s storage allowance.\nMembers pack unfinished projects into their allocated containers and add the next review date before leaving. Each member controls the arrangement within a clearly bounded storage allowance that others can identify.\nMembers reserve a storage position on the board before packing unfinished projects and labeling their next review dates. Knowing the available position helps members choose a container that fits before they clear the bench."
    }
  ],
